# Dependencies
# `node_modules` without a trailing slash, deliberately.
#
# `node_modules/` matches DIRECTORIES only. Genie is developed across parallel
# git worktrees whose `node_modules` is a LINK to the main checkout's, and a
# SYMLINK is not a directory to git — so it showed as untracked (`?? node_modules`)
# and one `git add -A` would have committed a link to an absolute local path.
# A junction happens to be ignored; a symlink was not. Both are ignored now.
node_modules

# Build output — Electron main, preload, and the renderer's static
# export. All of `app/` is generated by `npm run dev` (nextron) or by
# `npm run build` (electron-builder). Nothing in here is source.
app/

# Next.js dev cache + export
renderer/.next/
renderer/out/

# electron-builder release artifacts
dist/
release/
out/

# Per-user OS-service pty-host runtime — a BUILD ARTIFACT produced by
# scripts/build-service-runtime.mjs (standalone Node + ABI-matched node-pty).
# Regenerated per OS×arch in CI before packaging; never committed.
resources/runtime/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local environment overrides.
#
# `.env*` rather than an enumerated list: a stray `.env.testing` was found at
# this repo's root carrying DB_PASSWORD and APP_KEY — a Laravel env file, in the
# Electron repo, matching neither name below and therefore committable. An
# allow-list of env filenames only ignores the ones somebody thought of, and the
# cost of missing one is a credential in the history.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test coverage
coverage/
.vitest-cache/

# Playwright E2E output (reports + per-test artifacts)
test-results/
playwright-report/
.playwright/

# TypeScript incremental build state
*.tsbuildinfo
